              "type": "text",
              "text": "Search for and verify the paper \"The Format Tax\" (arXiv 2604.03616, April 2026). The claim is that it shows 92% of format-induced accuracy degradation originates at the PROMPT LEVEL (from schema complexity in the prompt forcing the model to simultaneously reason about content and satisfy structural constraints), not from decoder-level grammar masking (which contributes only ~1.6 pp additional loss). \n\nUse WebSearch to find this paper and WebFetch to read its abstract and key findings. Report:\n1. Does this paper exist?\n2. Does it actually claim 92% prompt-level vs ~1.6pp decoder-level?\n3. What tasks/benchmarks does it evaluate on?\n4. Any caveats or limitations that would affect its applicability to information extraction?\n\nBe concise in your report (under 300 words)."
            }
          ],
